            <ArticleTitle>Current Histopathologic and Molecular Characterisations of Prostate Cancer: Towards Individualised Prognosis and Therapies.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>186-90</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.eururo.2015.05.041</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0302-2838(15)00443-1</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Data on TMPRSS2-ERG and AR-V7 may pave the way for personalised therapy for prostate cancer (PCa) patients. Comprehensive molecular profiling can help identify multiple PCa subtypes and driving alterations. Translating these findings into clinical practice is still challenging.</AbstractText>
